{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-fvv-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d: the `process-evap-fvv` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm` -- the national tables and the onroad model -- and supplies the run's own selections and its expected output.\n\n`MultidayTankVaporVentingCalculator` WRITES ITS RATE IN TWO DISJOINT INSERTS, and this run reads one of them. TVV-8's operating insert takes `emissionRateByAge` at modes 150 and 300 and multiplies mode 300 by `tempAdj x rvpAdj`: a cubic in the ambient temperature (`evapTemperatureAdjustment`) and a cubic whose four terms are `evapRVPTemperatureAdjustment` interpolated at the fuel's TANK RVP. That RVP is `TankFuelGenerator`'s `averageTankGasoline`, which runs master-side, reaches no worker and is empty in every snapshot and in the default database, so the model computes it: the market-share means of TFG-1, the zone's evaporative temperature and the weathering of TFG-2, the commingling step of TFG-3 -- 8.0 psi for gasoline and 7.7 for E85 here, read at the ethanol volume AFTER `FuelEffectsGenerator`'s high-ethanol substitution, without which E85 would weather to 7.61. The RVP is the one input the answer is sensitive to on a run like this: docs/evap-fvv.md 0.3 measures +2 psi moving the total by 9.6 %.\n\nTHE OTHER INSERT IS NOT COMPUTED, and the document says so rather than implying otherwise. The cold-soak insert writes mode 151 from TVV-2 to TVV-7 -- the peak cold-soak hour, tank vapour generated at two altitudes, the multi-day soak fold, the venting equations -- and it is the only consumer of that chain. On an on-network link its operating-mode fraction is exactly 0, computed (E2's `1 - fractionOfOperating`, and `fractionOfOperating` is 1 because `SourceHours` is `SHO` there): the spec's reproduction computes the chain in full for this snapshot -- 1,344 cold-soak base rates, the largest 0.413 g/h -- and they contribute exactly 0. `run_offNetworkLinkCount` is asserted 0 by the shape check, so a RunSpec that selects road type 1 -- the one kind that would weight mode 151 -- fails loudly here instead of silently dropping the venting half.\n\nIT EMITS 64 ROWS -- 41 gasoline and 23 E85 model years, one block, a rectangle -- and all 64 reproduce at 7.517e-06 on the model's first run, the same worst cell the pandas reproduction from the national tables reached before the model changed.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "evaporative"
    ]
  },
